          unusual layouts. We understand these systems and diagnose airflow,
          ductwork, and furnace problems correctly.
        </p>

      </div>

      <div class="why-card">

        <h3>The Fraser Outflow is What Breaks Furnaces</h3>

        <p>
          Most of winter is mild, but when cold Fraser outflow winds arrive,
          heating systems suddenly work much harder. Weak igniters, motors,
          sensors, and other worn components often fail during these cold
          periods. Preventive repairs before winter can help avoid emergency
          breakdowns.
        </p>

      </div>

      <div class="why-card">

        <h3>Every Neighborhood is Different</h3>

        <p>
          Homes on Alabama Hill, South Hill, Silver Beach, Fairhaven, and
          Edgemoor all have different heating challenges. Some suffer from
          airflow imbalance while others struggle with oversized homes and long
          duct runs. We diagnose the actual cause instead of recommending
          unnecessary replacements.
        </p>

      </div>

      <div class="why-card">

        <h3>Local Response Times</h3>

        <p>
          Because Bellingham is our home base, we are able to respond quickly
          throughout the city. Most no-heat calls receive same-day scheduling,
          helping homeowners restore comfort as quickly as possible.
        </p>

